Digi Mono
---------
mods/digimono-st/upstream/ contains the unmodified Digi Mono engine from
gdeo607/digi1_mods, pinned at commit 32fd22a1fd66fa5833b808b1c1c049a0deb82d88.
It is MIT-licensed, copyright (c) 2026 the digi1_mods authors; its full licence
is included there. Its sine table is from Plaits (MIT, copyright 2016 Emilie
Gillet); the full notice is retained in upstream/sine.c. No MACRO engine or
Monomachine firmware is included. The original Syntakt adapters are GPL-2.0-or-later.

MONO2K
------
mods/digimono-st/mono2k/upstream/ contains source snapshots from MONO2K by
Inigo Hernandez (https://github.com/InigoHernandez/mono2k), pinned at commit
95d5763495d961f3ed225f5e4201328934ca4247, GPL-3.0-only. The full licence and
source hashes are included there. ENS and SID-6581 are extracted
from these clean-room generators, with tables regenerated for 48 kHz.
The new DSP, extraction script and combined AUDIO adapter are GPL-3.0-only;
the historical combined bank used GPL-3.0-only with MIT notices retained.
From Digi Mono 0.6.0, the FM+ replacement adds AGPLv3 terms (below).
No original Monomachine firmware is included or needed.

De-Pattern FM+
--------------
mods/digimono-st/fmplus/upstream/ pins De-Pattern/dn2mk2-firmware at
a0249fc55fd188242c92f377b4cbb2748b851a35 (AGPL-3.0-or-later), including
its full licence. fmplus.c is an integer port of its FM+ STAT/PAR/DYN.
The combined machine is distributed under AGPLv3 with all GPL/MIT notices
retained. The original FM tables are included as C arrays at the owner's
explicit request, with an OS 1.32B extraction recipe and source/output hashes.
No Elektron executable code or complete firmware is included.

Machine subtype selector
------------------------
elekloader/sdk/include/syntakt/subtype-picker.h adapts the GPL-2.0-or-later
MAIN UI and original small glyphs from the uncommitted Synfact MD prototype.
The source snapshot hashes and base revision are retained in
mods/digimono-st/picker-provenance.json; docs/SUBTYPE-PICKER.md describes the
adaptation. No mdkit/Machinedrum DSP or firmware is imported by this UI work.

Monomachine reference bench
--------------------------
tools/monomachine-reference/ builds an offline driver against Monomodule
(https://github.com/shnolk/monomodule, copyright Shnolk, AGPL-3.0), downloaded
separately at its recorded revision. reference.cpp/reference.cmake and compat.h
are AGPL-3.0-only; the Python tools and host adapter are GPL-3.0-only. The
included MinGW patch adjusts the Windows calling convention in the separately
downloaded GPLv3 DSP56300 emulator; it does not change DSP opcode semantics.
Upstream dependency notices are retained in their checkouts. No Monomachine OS,
extracted firmware, reference recording or generated JIT code is included here.

Elektron
--------
Elektron, Digitakt, Digitone, Syntakt and Analog are trademarks of Elektron
Music Machines. elekloader is not affiliated with or endorsed by Elektron.
It contains no Elektron firmware and distributes nothing derived from it:
every build happens on the user's machine, from the stock OS file the user
supplies. Mods carry only their authors' own bytes, plus short instruction
fragments needed to hook the OS (runs of stock bytes under 8 bytes long, and
the instructions a hook displaces, are stored as they are), and hashes of
the stock bytes they expect.
